## Why This Is Asked
Assesses how a candidate combines deployment strategies, DR planning, and enforcement of security/compliance in a real GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Blue/Green and canary deployments with automatic rollback gates
- Cross-region DR for compute and database
- CMEK encryption for storage and Cloud SQL
- Policy-as-code and drift detection (Config Connector, OPA)
- Observability, outage handling, and compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for SLO gate
async function canaryGate(metrics) {
  const latencyOk = metrics.p95 < 200;
  const errorOk = metrics.errorRate < 0.01;
  return latencyOk && errorOk;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate drift detection in CI/CD and ensure fast remediations?
- What tests would you run to validate cross-region failover without customer-visible downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical multi-region rollout safety using native tools and a rapid rollback kill switch, a realistic DevOps constraint.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Run traffic management and per-revision routing
- Cloud Monitoring alerting for latency, errors, and resource pressure
- Cloud Functions as an automated kill switch trigger
- Artifact Registry integration with Cloud Run
- Minimal IAM permissions for automated rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Cloud Function: killSwitch.js
exports.killSwitch = (req, res) => {
  // Pseudo: switch all traffic to v1 100%
  // gcloud run services update-traffic data-processor --to-revisions data-processor-v1=100
  res.status(200).send('Kill switch activated: traffic routed to v1');
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the kill switch without affecting live users?
- Which alert thresholds would you tune for a gradual rollout vs immediate kill switch activation?
